'' A float macro is written with the shortest spelling that reads back as the same double:
'' 'str( d )' stopped at 16 digits, so DBL_MAX came back INF and 0.1 + 0.2 came back 0.3
'' (audit F-50).
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -cimport tests/cimport/src/floatmac.h -cimport-out -
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: 1.7976931348623157e+308
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0.30000000000000004
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0.1
'' EXPECT-OUT: 0.5
